@startuml
' Rendered by scripts/build-diagrams.sh. Edit this file, never the SVG beside it.
' The colours, the fonts and the transparent ground come from palette.iuml.
!include palette.iuml

' What earns this picture is that the three questions are one gate rather than a
' checklist. Any single yes ends it, none of them outranks another, and there is
' one way out, which is the thing prose spells out worst: read as three
' paragraphs, they look like three considerations to weigh against each other.
'
' One diamond carrying three lines rather than three diamonds in a row, and the
' answer on the edge rather than in the box. Three diamonds would draw an order
' that does not exist, and would repeat the same outcome three times, which reads
' as three different outcomes at a glance.
'
' The second half is here rather than in its own picture because it only ever
' runs after the first: the title test is asked about a card that has already
' absorbed something, and the divergence is written once, at the end, in the pull
' request rather than in the card.
'
' Separate from card-lifecycle.puml on purpose. That one draws a card's states and
' the edge a finished lot runs back to the next one; this one draws a decision
' taken inside one of those states. Folding them together would put nine more
' edges around the loop that diagram exists to show, and drown it.
'
' No actor. The person doing the work is in every box here, so drawing them adds
' a lane and says nothing. Entirely grey for the same reason as its sibling:
' nothing here is an owner or a refusal, which is what colour is for in this set.
'
' The split into one or more pull requests is deliberately absent. It is decided
' once, later, on the branch's git log rather than on any single piece of work,
' so it belongs to a different moment than this one.

start
:Something turns up\nwhile the card is open;

if (Does it finish in this session?\nDoes it need a decision you would not make alone?\nDoes it touch a migration or the published contract?) then (any yes)
  :A card of its own;
  stop
else (all no)
endif

:Done in this card,\nin its own commit;

if (Is the card's title\nstill true?) then (yes)
  :The scope grew.\nThe body is adjusted;
else (no)
  :The goal changed.\nThe card is rewritten,\nor closed;
endif

:Why the original plan was wrong\ngoes in the pull request;
stop
@enduml
